Year = {2020},
Note = {IEEE Global Communications Conference (GLOBECOM) on Advanced Technology
   for 5G Plus, ELECTR NETWORK, DEC 07-11, 2020},
Organization = {IEEE; IEEE Commun Soc; Chunghwa Telecom; Foxconn; Huawei; Mediatek; 6G
   Off; Askey; Ericsson; FET Qualcomm; Taiwan Mobile; Auden Techno Corp;
   Keysight Technologies; Telecom Technol Ctr; NI},
Abstract = {Internet of vehicles (IoV) is an eminent road-side communication
   assistive technology that is designed to meet the service requirements
   of the users. As autonomous vehicles are the base for IoV environment,
   selecting authenticated neighbours is a prime task for improving the
   security of the communication environment. In this article,
   classification based trust model (CTM) for IoV is designed for improving
   the detection and verification of data and vehicles in the dynamic
   scenario. The classification and verification follows naive Bayes
   machine learning model for distinguishing the vehicles as trusted and
   untrusted. Depending on the communication attributes of the vehicles,
   classification distribution is modelled for direct trust in both
   independent and joint manner. The proposed model is assessed using
   simulation experiments and it is seen that this model achieves fair
   trusted and untrusted vehicle detection and less verification delay.},
